      "created_at": "2018-09-25T21:39:07Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-09-25T21:39:07Z",
      "body": "Well, I'd be fine with \"on\" by default. Because there is no interactive installer.\r\nIf, and only if, this is not some kind of passive sniffing of the usage.\r\nWe all know what privacy concerns are, and you seem to fairly understand this. (cf https://github.com/traccar/traccar-client-android/commit/cbfe90757d6ff3c670485dacc76a2165125f9a06#diff-c8cc2dd42271f2bf39c6aa81eb6a5529)\r\nJust don't know what it sends exactly, I had no time to look at this part of the code.\r\nOn the other hand, it seems that some statistics are available through the API, correct ?\r\nAre they the same ?\r\nWhat is the usage exactly ? (traccar.org is the default destination).\r\nI'm ok sending relevant statistics (àla popcon: when you install Debian you are asked if you do want to contribute, but there is no text or graphical installer, in Traccar's case).\r\nAnd there are a whole lot of nice things to graph about the server usage, I could list tens if needed.\r\nOne that I'd like to see is some kind of \"device protocol market share\", for instance.\r\nMy 2c.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
