      "created_at": "2018-09-25T21:45:29Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-09-25T21:45:29Z",
      "body": "Statistics include the same information that you see on the \"Statistics\" screen in the web app. It's information such as total number of active devices and users. It also includes version number of the server, so we can see what percentage of servers use which version. I'm happy to share it publicly in some kind of graph, but just haven't had any time to implement it.\r\n\r\nI want to note that it's completely different from Firebase analytics. We have full control in this case, we know what's uploaded and we never share it with any third party. As for Firebase, it's only included in the apps available from the stores, so if you download binaries from website or build it yourself, you won't have any analytics.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
