      "created_at": "2018-09-26T20:01:53Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-09-26T20:04:44Z",
      "body": "I do not want to take part for anyone.\r\n\r\n1. The option of opting in or out is not possible right now, for the installer is non-interactive. Let me mention Debian again, their popcon is just like that: at install time you are asked whether you want to contribute (anonymously) submitting statistics, or not. Then you install the OS. Traccar's installer has room for improvement, but a windozlikegraphicalassistantformymom would not be my priority.\r\n2. I took a quick look at the code, and if those statistics are the same you get in the interface, well, they look quite innocuous to me. Sad point is that they are (not yet) exploited, nor available to all, be it through a dashboard or a plain html table on the website. It was not documented, now it is. \r\n(2b. Also, it is not like the Hidden Client). \r\n3. Having worked for companies that sold DPI software to some dictators you'd just hate me, well, let's not exaggerate. When their surveillance probes would \"phone home\", it was deeply embedded in some encrypted C-shared object. Not something really easy to grep or reverse.\r\n(3b. Ever heard of Google ?) ",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
